# Halo: Combat Evolved (4D530004), Nova. Built from the generic survey
# 1790933948-titleroutes-171581 (lane.titleroutes session 65, read by
# lane.titleroutes2 session 1, 2026-10-02). Read from its route-frames,
# not guessed:
#   boot20 (031011): the Bungie logo; boot40/booted (031032, 031054): the
#     main menu, CAMPAIGN lit.
#   cycle 1 (031100 START / 031106 A): START picks CAMPAIGN -> ENTER NAME
#     with the default "New001" and the cursor on Done; A takes it ->
#     CHOOSE DIFFICULTY, NORMAL lit.
#   cycle 2 (031111 START / 031117 A): START picks Normal -> LOADING; black.
#   cycle 3 (031123 START / 031129 A): black, then "Reveille": the cryo bay,
#     the tech at his console. Live and player-controlled.
#   cycles 4-14: START opens the pause panel (RESUME GAME lit; objective
#     "Complete training diagnostic") and A resumes. The tip "Use RIGHT
#     [stick] to look around" stays up the whole time: the look training
#     waits for up/down look input, and the survey only ever sent RX.
#   play (031405-031456): the same room with the camera swung right.
# So: 5 START/A cycles (3 reached the cryo bay; 2 guard pairs are pause +
# resume), then a training block that looks up, down, left and right on
# the RIGHT stick and walks on the LEFT stick, three times over (so the
# training's order does not matter), mark, then a walk loop with no START.
# A is jump and X is action in play; B (melee) and A also answer an
# "invert the look?" question either way, which does not change the run.
# The survey made a "New001" profile; if the title now lists profiles
# first, START/A pick the lit one, so the cycle count should hold -- the
# frames will say. NOT YET REPLAYED. What a pass looks like: the play
# frames leave the cryo bay (corridors of the Pillar of Autumn), not five
# minutes of one room.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
shot booted
repeat 5 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
repeat 3 {
    axis RY min
    wait 1.5
    axis RY mid
    wait 2
    axis RY max
    wait 1.5
    axis RY mid
    wait 2
    axis RX max
    wait 0.8
    axis RX mid
    wait 1
    axis RX min
    wait 0.8
    axis RX mid
    wait 1
    press B
    wait 2
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    axis LY mid
    wait 2
    shot training
}
mark gameplay               # CHECK: player control past the look training, no pause panel
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 4
    press X
    wait 0.5
    axis RX max
    wait 0.5
    axis RX mid
    wait 3
    press A
    wait 1
    axis RX min
    wait 0.9
    axis RX mid
    wait 3
    axis LY mid
    axis LX max
    wait 1
    axis LX mid
    axis LY min
    wait 3
    axis LY mid
    shot play
}
